# Archify & STMR Universal Architecture Visualizer (Cursor Rule)

Teach Cursor to analyze any codebase or ingest PRD/BRD documents, extract its system architecture into the **STMR (System-Topic-Module-Relationship)** model, and compile a self-contained, interactive HTML visualizer with Figma-grade design.

## 1. Attribution & Metadata
- **Author**: `Manik Prabhu` (`Senior Marketing and Delivery Manager`)
- **Company / Organization**: `Digio Click` (`DJOClick`)
- **Visualizer Header/Footer**: Displays `Manik Prabhu | Senior Marketing and Delivery Manager | Digio Click`

## 2. Dual-Mode Triggering & Ingestion
- **PRD / BRD Ingestion**: Ingests requirements specifications to generate cloud, frontend, backend, data, and queue architecture.
- **Codebase Scanning**: Inspects directories, configs (Docker, K8s, Terraform), and controllers to extract live system maps.

## 3. Explicit Cloud Infrastructure & Managed Services
- Every generated architecture must explicitly declare the Cloud Provider (**AWS**, **Azure**, **GCP**, or **Kubernetes/Hybrid**).
- Catalogues specific cloud services (e.g. AWS S3, ECS, ECR, EKS, DynamoDB; Azure Cosmos DB, Functions, AKS; GCP Cloud Run, GKE, Spanner).
- Renders official vector SVG cloud and technology icons in Figma-styled cards.

## 4. Concrete Module Technical Specs & Endpoints
- Exact runtime and frameworks (e.g. Node.js 22 + TypeScript 5.8, Python 3.12 + FastAPI, React 19).
- Exact exposed REST/gRPC endpoints with HTTP method pills (`GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `DELETE`).
- Slide-over inspection drawer for deep dive module contracts.
